<style>
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 12px 0; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-grid { display: inline-block; margin-right: 24px; vertical-align: middle; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-grid-row { display: flex; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-cell { width: 54px; height: 42px; margin: 2px; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-cell.selected { background: #1686bb; color: white; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-chart { min-height: 300px; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab img { max-width: 100%; }
    #pinput_shaping_tab .pinput-position { display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; }
</style>

<div id="pinput_shaping_tab">
    <h3>Input Shaping</h3>
    <p>Calibrate one axis at a time. The printer profile supplies travel limits.
        Secure the sensor, clear the bed and keep the stop control accessible.</p>

    <div class="alert alert-info" aria-live="polite">
        Input shaping: <strong data-bind="text: firmware().label"></strong>
        (<span data-bind="text: firmware().state"></span>).
        <span data-bind="text: firmware().message"></span>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: detectFirmware, enable: available">Detect firmware</button>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-error" role="alert" data-bind="visible: error, text: error"></div>
    <div class="alert alert-info" data-bind="visible: summary, text: summary"></div>
    <div class="alert alert-warning" data-bind="visible: recoveryRequired">
        A calibration was interrupted. Native motion may still be active; stop and settings must be verified before another test.
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: recover, enable: !busy() &amp;&amp; printerState.isOperational()">Restore saved settings</button>
    </div>
    <div class="alert alert-info" data-bind="visible: nativeSelected">
        Native Marlin M495: <strong data-bind="text: nativeCapability().state"></strong>.
        <span data-bind="text: nativeCapability().message"></span>
        Configure and detect support in Settings before calibration. Marlin uses its internal test position;
        the position grid applies to axis checks and software calibration.
    </div>
    <div data-bind="if: diagnostics() &amp;&amp; !result()">
        <p>Native run diagnostics: <code data-bind="text: diagnostics().session_id"></code></p>
        <p data-bind="foreach: Object.keys(diagnostics().files)">
            <a data-bind="text: $data, attr: {href: $root.fileURL($data)}"></a> ·
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pinput-actions">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: prepareModes, enable: available">Prepare coordinate modes</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: runAccTest, enable: available">Sensor values</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { runAxisTest('X'); }, enable: canMove">Test X axis</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: function () { runAxisTest('Y'); }, enable: canMove">Test Y axis</button>
        <button class="btn btn-warning" data-bind="click: cancel, enable: busy">Cancel test</button>
        <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: emergencyStop, enable: printerState.isOperational">Stop printer (M112)</button>
    </div>
    <p data-bind="visible: !modesReady()">Prepare coordinate modes before commanding calibration motion.</p>
    <p data-bind="visible: !firmwareReady()">Calibration and result application require a compatible detected firmware.</p>
    <p aria-live="polite" data-bind="visible: busy">
        Stage: <strong data-bind="text: stage"></strong>
        <span data-bind="visible: progress"> — <span data-bind="text: progress"></span>%</span>
        <span data-bind="text: progressSource"></span>.
        Sensor: <span data-bind="text: sensorState"></span>
    </p>

    <table class="table table-condensed" data-bind="visible: samples().length">
        <thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>X</th><th>Y</th><th>Z</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-bind="foreach: samples">
            <tr><td data-bind="text: time"></td><td data-bind="text: x"></td>
                <td data-bind="text: y"></td><td data-bind="text: z"></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <hr>
    <h4>Calibration position</h4>
    <div class="pinput-grid" data-bind="foreach: grid">
        <div class="pinput-grid-row" data-bind="foreach: $data">
            <button class="btn pinput-cell" data-bind="text: (row * 3 + col + 1),
                css: {selected: $root.selectedCell().row === row &amp;&amp; $root.selectedCell().col === col},
                enable: $root.available, click: function () { $root.selectedCell($data); },
                attr: {'aria-label': 'Select row ' + (row + 1) + ', column ' + (col + 1)}"></button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pinput-position">
        <label for="pinput-z">Z height (mm)</label>
        <input id="pinput-z" type="number" min="10" step="1" class="input-small"
            data-bind="value: selectedZ, attr: {max: sizeZ}, enable: available">
        <p>X: <span data-bind="text: calculatedX"></span> mm,
            Y: <span data-bind="text: calculatedY"></span> mm</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pinput-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: function () { runResonance('X'); }, enable: canCalibrate">Calibrate X</button>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: function () { runResonance('Y'); }, enable: canCalibrate">Calibrate Y</button>
    </div>

    <div data-bind="visible: result">
        <hr>
        <h4>Measured result</h4>
        <p data-bind="with: result">
            Backend: <span data-bind="text: backend || 'software'"></span>.
            Axis <strong data-bind="text: axis"></strong>:
            resonance <strong data-bind="text: base_freq !== null ? base_freq.toFixed(1) : 'No confident candidate'"></strong> Hz.
            Recommended <strong data-bind="text: best_shaper"></strong>
            at <strong data-bind="text: best_shaper_freq !== null ? best_shaper_freq.toFixed(1) : 'Unavailable'"></strong> Hz.
        </p>
        <div data-bind="if: result() &amp;&amp; result().backend === 'marlin_m495'">
            <div data-bind="with: result().quality">
                <p data-bind="with: $data.alignment">
                    Excitation interval estimated from the signal:
                    <span data-bind="text: sensor_start.toFixed(2)"></span>–<span data-bind="text: sensor_end.toFixed(2)"></span> s;
                    boundary uncertainty ±<span data-bind="text: uncertainty_seconds.toFixed(2)"></span> s.
                </p>
                <p>Supported fundamental coverage: <span data-bind="text: (coverage * 100).toFixed(1)"></span>%.</p>
                <ul data-bind="foreach: $data.resonance_candidates || []">
                    <li>Candidate resonance: <span data-bind="text: frequency.toFixed(1)"></span> ±
                        <span data-bind="text: uncertainty_hz.toFixed(1)"></span> Hz;
                        relative power <span data-bind="text: relative_power.toFixed(1)"></span>.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <table class="table table-striped">
            <thead><tr><th>Shaper</th><th>Frequency (Hz)</th><th>Predicted residual</th>
                <th>Duration (ms)</th><th>Theoretical accel limit (mm/s²)</th><th>Recommended</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-bind="foreach: shapers">
                <tr><td data-bind="text: name"></td><td data-bind="text: frequency"></td>
                    <td data-bind="text: vibration"></td><td data-bind="text: duration"></td>
                    <td data-bind="text: acceleration"></td><td data-bind="text: best ? 'Yes' : ''"></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="alert alert-warning" data-bind="with: result">
            <ul data-bind="foreach: warnings"><li data-bind="text: $data"></li></ul>
        </div>
        <label for="pinput-shaper">Shaper to apply</label>
        <select id="pinput-shaper" data-bind="options: shaperChoices, optionsText: 'label', optionsValue: 'name',
            value: selectedShaper, valueAllowUnset: true, enable: canSelectShaper"></select>
        <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: useRecommendation, enable: canSelectShaper">Use recommendation</button>
        <p>FTM allows any fitted shaper from this measurement. Each choice uses its saved frequency and damping.
            Legacy firmware supports ZV only.</p>
        <p><code data-bind="text: selectedCommand"></code></p>
        <button class="btn btn-success" data-bind="click: applyResult, enable: canApply, text: applyLabel"></button>
        <p>Settings are applied to the tested axis in RAM. Validate with a print before saving them to EEPROM.</p>
        <p><a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('csv')}">Download raw CSV</a></p>
        <p data-bind="visible: result() &amp;&amp; result().backend === 'marlin_m495'">
            <a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('events')}">Protocol events</a> ·
            <a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('excitation')}">Excitation and cleanup</a> ·
            <a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('analysis')}">Analysis diagnostics</a> ·
            <a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('metadata')}">Sensor metadata</a> ·
            <a data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('sensor_log')}">Sensor log</a>
        </p>

        <div id="pinput_signal" class="pinput-chart" data-bind="visible: interactiveAvailable"></div>
        <div id="pinput_psd" class="pinput-chart" data-bind="visible: interactiveAvailable"></div>
        <h5>Signal and predicted spectra</h5>
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('signal')}">
            <img alt="Captured acceleration signal" data-bind="attr: {src: fileURL('signal')}">
        </a>
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-bind="attr: {href: fileURL('psd')}">
            <img alt="Measured spectrum and predicted shaper responses" data-bind="attr: {src: fileURL('psd')}">
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Interactive charts are optional; PNG plots and result application work offline. -->
<script src="https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-3.0.1.min.js" charset="utf-8" async
    onload="window.dispatchEvent(new Event('pinputPlotlyReady'))"></script>
